# Auto commit and push

After finishing a meaningful set of code changes in this project, **commit and push to `origin` on the current branch without waiting for the user to ask**.

Follow the existing git safety protocol:
- Never update git config
- Never force-push to main/master unless explicitly requested
- Never commit secrets (`.env`, credentials) or `server/uploads/`
- Use a concise commit message focused on why
- Run status/diff/log before committing; push after a successful commit
- Skip empty commits when there is nothing to push
